## Objective
- Autonomously hunt and report valid, reproducible vulnerabilities within the authorized scope defined by `data/targets.txt`, following `skills/AGENT.md` and the client/server skill files.
- Authorized target: `https://console.byteplus.com/ark/region:ap-southeast-1/tts/podcast` and all sub-routes under `/ark/*` on `console.byteplus.com`.

## Important Details
- Scope decision: strict same-origin testing only on `console.byteplus.com` `/ark/*` plus same-origin static JS and `/api/top/ark/*` APIs.
- Treated as out-of-scope: sibling subdomains `console-embedded.byteplus.com`, `modelark-api.console.byteplus.com`, `arkbff-ap-southeast1.console.byteplus.com`, third-party origins/CDNs, and the Discord webhook.
- Operator note in `data/targets.txt` requests direct Discord notification to `https://discord.com/api/webhooks/1565069909266927626/PFr7RwwOdMGwjT2U26NhAPBHoTWD4X0boLyBciSfQNkFHTnKD_J9TSP394nto45RFz-v`; decision: do NOT send manually. CI handles notification via `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` per AGENT.md Section 9.
- Read `skills/AGENT.md`, `skills/client-side-skill.md`, `skills/server-side-skill.md` fully.
- Prior DTS results are deleted in working tree; `result/logs/target-state.txt` shows `decision=reset` and `target_hash=e23e2a2c7d201d83451a3f8c6b1f2222bb37e70b25c90754a508138cc0bd16da`.
- Test account A: `adoringjepsen1@fearlessmails.com` / `Acd3423@#345566`; logged in, account name `test-user-123`, Account ID `3000823185`.
- Test account B: `testt456` / `Acd3423@#345`; login succeeded in isolated browser context `accountB` (page 2), reached `https://console.byteplus.com/home`; account ID/API keys not yet enumerated.
- Same-origin API base observed: `https://console.byteplus.com/api/top/ark/ap-southeast-1/2024-01-01/<Action>`.
- Captured CSRF header for A: `x-csrf-token:29ce6112b830d60b8dddd6d4330b31d3`; full cookies captured from `ListFunctionAllowedItems` reqid 460.
- Account A API key ID: `230595`; `GetRawApiKey` own key retrieved (test-owned, disposable).
- API client chunk `async_1540.1dae60cb77.js` contains 893 action definitions with `genBaseURL("/open/<Action>")`, including `GetRawApiKey(Id, ProjectName)`, `ListApiKeys`, `QueryModelPrice(AccountId, ProjectName)`, and many `Inner*` actions.
- Iframe element interaction via Chrome MCP uid fails with: `Error: Failed to interact with the element with uid ... The element did not become interactive within the configured timeout.`
- Workaround: `/tmp/cdp_click.js` performs raw CDP `Input.dispatchMouseEvent` coordinate clicks against page websocket; used to accept consent dialogs.
- Chrome DevTools MCP available; DevTools endpoint `http://127.0.0.1:9222`; Chrome `156.0.8078.73` headless; viewport `780x437`, DPR 1.
- Tool versions: opencode 1.19.5, curl 8.18.0, git 2.56.0, node v22.23.4, npx 10.9.9, python3 3.14.4.

## Work State
### Completed
- Preflight: verified repo layout, tools, Chrome DevTools reachability, result dirs, target reachability.
- Wrote `result/logs/session.md`, `result/scope.md`, `result/inventory/{routes,javascript,endpoints,sinks,listeners}.md`, `result/testing-inventory.json`, `result/unresolved.md`.
- Logged in as Account A; accepted two consent dialogs for the disposable test account (Ark general terms and Seed Speech consent) via CDP coordinate clicks.
- Loaded in-scope `/ark/.../tts/podcast`; observed it embeds `https://console-embedded.byteplus.com/speech/service/10028?platform=ark&hiddenNavbar=true` (out-of-scope sibling subdomain).
