## Objective
- Autonomously hunt and report valid, reproducible vulnerabilities under `/ark/*` on `console.byteplus.com` per `data/targets.txt` and `skills/AGENT.md`, writing confirmed findings to `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` (CI performs Discord notification).

## Important Details
- Scope: strict same-origin only — `console.byteplus.com` `/ark/*` routes plus same-origin `/api/top/ark/*` APIs and static JS on `res.gcloudcache.com/bp-fe/console-ark/ark-new-main/`.
- Out-of-scope: `console-embedded.byteplus.com`, `modelark-api.console.byteplus.com`, `arkbff-ap-southeast1.console.byteplus.com`, third-party CDNs, the Discord webhook. Do not send Discord notification manually.
- Test Account A: `adoringjepsen1@fearlessmails.com` / `Acd3423@#345566`; Account ID `3000823185`; API key Id `230595` (SID `apikey-20260827022328-88djq`).
- Test Account B (isolated context `accountB`, page 2): `testt456` / `Acd3423@#345`; Account ID `3001021825`.
- Same-origin API base: `https://console.byteplus.com/api/top/ark/ap-southeast-1/2024-01-01/<Action>`; CSRF via `x-csrf-token` header read from `csrfToken` cookie (not HttpOnly; same-origin `fetch` with `credentials:'include'` works).
- Gateway only exposes whitelisted public actions; all `Inner*`/internal actions tested return `InvalidActionOrVersion` (CodeN 100008).
- Client-side chunks base: `https://res.gcloudcache.com/bp-fe/console-ark/ark-new-main/`; chunk URL pattern `static/js/async/<id>.<hash>.js`.
- `ArkBffService` (e.g. `GetAccountMeta`, `ListModels`) lives on `arkbff-ap-southeast1.console.byteplus.com/api/2024-10-01` — out of scope; `GetAccountMeta` accepts arbitrary `AccountId`/`IncludeBalance` but cannot be tested.
- MCP uid clicks fail inside cross-origin iframes; use `/tmp/cdp_click.js` raw CDP coordinate clicks (Chrome DevTools endpoint `http://127.0.0.1:9222`, Chrome 156 headless, viewport 780x437).
- Prior DTS finding (`DTS-INFO-001`, low info disclosure) only visible via `git show HEAD:...`; not persisted and not relevant to Ark.
- `result/logs/target-state.txt`: `decision=reset`, target hash `e23e2a2c7d201d83451a3f8c6b1f2222bb37e70b25c90754a508138cc0bd16da`.

## Work State
### Completed
- Logged in both accounts; A accepted Ark general terms + Seed Speech consent.
- Downloaded ~38 JS chunks to `/tmp/arkjs` (incl. `async_1540.1dae60cb77.js` = 893 `/open/<Action>` defs; `async_async-main.d0a27388a1.js` route map; `async_7006.3374811d72.js` iframe shell; `async_9485.307dc84e28.js` media asset service; `async_6652`/`async_9764` postMessage lib) and remote entries to `/tmp/arkremote`.
- Route map extracted: `/overview`, `/apiKey`, `/usageTracking`, `/projectManagement`, `/openManagement`, `/security`, `/vpc`, `/dataset`, `/endpoint`, `/customModel`, `/batchInference`, `/finetune`, `/eval`, `/assistant`, `/application/*`, `/experience/*`, `/tts/{podcast,tts2,soundReplicate,timbreDesign,speechRecognition,recordingRecognition,realTimeRecognition,simulS2S}`, `/model`, `/gallery`, `/arkcli`, `/tokenCalculator`, `/subscription/*`, `/pickupVoucher`, `/model-settings/*`, `/ipDashboard/*`, `/inferenceFoundry`, `/autope/*`.
- IDOR/BOLA negatives on `/api/top/ark/ap-southeast-1/2024-01-01`:
  - `GetRawApiKey`: A→B key `300439` = `NotFound.Id`; B→A key `230595` = `NotFound.Id`; variants `Id:"300439"`, `[300439]`, `{Id:300439}` = `InvalidParameter.Id`; float `300439.0` = `NotFound.Id`.
  - `UpdateApiKey` A on B key `300439` = `NotFound.Id`.
  - `DeleteApiKey` only works on own keys.
  - `ListApiKeys`: account-scoped (`AccountId` field in response reflects caller; B sees only own).
  - `CreateApiKey` mass assignment `AccountId:3001021825` ignored — key `300453` created under A `3000823185`, tag `sys:ark:createdBy=Root/3000823185`.
  - `CreateApiKey` with nonexistent `ProjectName:'b-proj-20261030'` = `NotFound.ProjectName`; no project-create API in Ark JS (IAM out of scope) → project-name confusion not testable.
  - `GetApiKeySecurityConfig`/`UpdateApiKeySecurityConfig` account-scoped: toggled A true, B remained false; A reverted to false.
  - `QueryModelPrice` with `AccountId` A/B/1 → identical public pricing (AccountId ignored).
  - `GetAccountInfo` with extra `AccountId` → returns caller's AccountId (ignored).
  - `GetInferenceUsage`, `GetModelChargeItem`, `ListDataCollectionPermissions`, `GetAutoSetFreeLimit`, `ListAccountQuotas`, `ListSeatInfos`, `ListSubscribeTrade`, `GetSeatInfo`, `GetAccountAgreement`, `ListModelChargeItems` observed; all session-scoped, no `AccountId` accepted.
  - `CreateMediaAssetGroup` under 2024-01-01 = `InvalidActionOrVersion`; media asset service version unknown.
- Cleanup done: deleted A key `300453` and B key `300439`.
- Client-side review negatives:
  - `RouteJump` postMessage handler (`async_6652`) gated by origin check in `async_9764` (`if("*"!==n&&e.origin!==n)return;`) — not exploitable.
  - iframe `navigate` message handler (`async_7006`) validates `https:` protocol, no userinfo, and origin equals sender or mapped `console.byteplus.com` — safe.
  - `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` banner sink in `overview_page.js` fed by server config, not attacker input.
  - `?env=`, `bytecloud_control_plane`, `projectName`, `Id` query params: only link propagation / known-site selection / canonical URL with regex — no sink.
- Wrote `result/logs/session.md`, `result/scope.md`, inventory skeletons, `result/testing-inventory.json`, `result/unresolved.md`.

### Active
- Exploring newer routes for same-origin actions with free, test-owned objects (last navigation: A → `https://console.byteplus.com/ark/region:ap-southeast-1/application/claw`, result not yet captured).
- Hunting a high-impact BAC/IDOR on same-origin `/api/top/ark/...`; available test objects limited to API keys (protected) and potentially free objects (bots/chains/media asset groups/agents) if their create actions are exposed.
- B page now on `/ark/region:ap-southeast-1/notfound` but same-origin fetches still work.

### Blocked
- Core `/tts/podcast` functionality lives in out-of-scope `console-embedded.byteplus.com/speech/service/10028`; limits depth on TTS/media-asset paths.
- No seats, subscriptions, projects, datasets, or endpoints in either test account; `GetSeatInfo(SeatID)`, media asset, and seat/subscription IDOR tests require creating paid resources.
- `ark_media_asset` service base URL/version not yet determined (chunk `async_9485.307dc84e28.js` has no version string).
- `Inner*` and internal actions rejected by gateway (`InvalidActionOrVersion`).
- MCP uid clicks fail in cross-origin iframes; only CDP coordinate clicks work.

## Next Move
1. Capture `/ark/region:ap-southeast-1/application/claw` network requests (same-origin `/api/top/ark/*`) and inspect create/list actions for bots/chains/agents that are free and reversible, then use them as cross-account IDOR test objects between A and B.
2. If no new actionable same-origin surface, record all negative results in `result/inventory/endpoints.md` + `result/unresolved.md`, update `result/testing-inventory.json`, and conclude (no `confirmed-vuln.txt` entry).

